SUMMARY:Weiqi/Go Teaching and Demonstrating
DESCRIPTION:The Portland Go Club provides interactive teachings on the rules\, strategies\, and history of Weiqi. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n11 AM – 1 PM | Every 3rd Sunday\, April 19 – September 20\, 2026 \n\n\n\nWeiqi\, also known as Go\, holds the distinction of being the oldest continuously played strategy game globally\, with origins dating back at least 3\,500 years. While its rules can be grasped in mere minutes\, the game’s strategies and historical significance are vast. As part of our ongoing cultural programs\, the Portland Go Club will provide teachings and demonstrations on the rules\, strategies\, and history of Weiqi\, considered one of the four traditional Scholarly Arts. Attendees will have the opportunity to observe live demonstrations and engage in Weiqi gameplay with volunteers from the Portland Go Club. \n\n\n\n\nGet Admission\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout the Portland Go Club\n\n\n\nThe Portland Go Club\, established in 1977\, has been facilitating Go/Weiqi meetups and events for nearly 50 years in the Portland area. The club hosts two weekly gatherings for players of all skill levels to play and learn about the game and its strategies. PGC hosts various community events including an annual Statewide tournament\, workshops taught by Professional Weiqi players\, educational tabling at cultural events\, and workshops for new players. We welcome players of all experience levels and are happy to teach new players at any of our meetups. \n\n\n\n\nLearn more\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/weiqi-go-teaching-and-demonstrating-3/2026-04-19/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Free with admission or membership
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/weichi-in-the-garden_2.webp
END:VEVENT
